  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "th_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -334
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Hand Theremin\n\nPlay it with your hand: switch Camera on and raise one hand to the webcam — left and right is pitch, up and down is loudness, and the tone sounds while your hand is in view. No camera? Hold the mouse button down over the preview and move instead. Snap on keeps you in the Scale (choose one on the canvas); off, it glides through every pitch like a real theremin, with vibrato.\n\nHow it works: Landmarks (hands) gives 21 points per hand; point 8 is the index fingertip. Select takes it while a hand is detected, else the mouse. Scale in range mode turns left–right into a note, Smooth glides between notes, an LFO adds vibrato and MIDI → Freq turns the note into Hz. Two oscillators (an octave apart) → Mix → Gain (the volume) → filter → delay → reverb. The rings pulse at a rate that follows the pitch; the string swells round the hand (Noise in `gaussian` mode) and ripples along.",
        "width": 470,
        "height": 270
      }
    },
